+## Turn usage (issue #93)
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the sum of input, output, and total tokens from every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call across two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L59)).
+- Rounds without usage contribute nothing to the sum; a turn with no reported usage receives `undefined`, including after a metered turn on the same orchestrator ([validated by: counts reported rounds around missing usage and reports nothing for an unmetered turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L70)).
+
+The selected contract keeps the existing usage argument and sums its three token fields. A named turn-total type and parameter must make this meaning visible in the public hook signature. Returning a per-round breakdown was rejected because provider-call granularity is not required for turn billing and would widen the consumer API. A direct answer retains its existing usage unchanged, as pinned by the existing `receives collected response text and usage` test in `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts`. This observable change requires a MINOR version bump and a changelog entry explaining that tool-heavy turns now report larger, complete totals.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The following property remains unchanged by issue #93.
 
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
